                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b] Update [/b]: so...I guess it's a little bit late since the update for StartBolita Green Box was late September, but here's an update:\nThink of the Green box as a new game that the developer gave to people who already owned the original Startbolita... but here's the plot twist: the new game isn't actually a normal marble game but an puzzle game where you control a marble and you need to put the cubes in the designed spots!\n\n\n[h1] Pros:\t[/h1]\n+ It has solid controls\n+ The puzzles are well thought\n+ The puzzles are challenging (at least for me, since I don't play often this type of puzzle games)\n+ After you pass a level you trully have the sense of accomplishment\n+ Achievements!\n+ The original Startbolita is still avaiable to play\n\n[h1] Cons:[/h1]\n- The original StartBolita is still crap\n- I think puzzles could use a little bit more  diversity with introduction of new mechanics (for example, adding some  mechanics since you're still playing with a marble, because in the current state, if you played with a marble or a cube like in GooCubelets, the puzzles would work the same) \n\n[b] Do I recommend it?[/b]\n[b] Yes,[/b] but only for people who like puzzle games since the original Startbolita didn't have any improvement.\n\n[b] It's worth the full price?\t[/b]\n[b] No.[/b] Although it contains 2 games, I value the original Startbolita at 1 euro tops. Although the Green Box it's a good puzzle game the rivalry at puzzle games is pretty big and we see games of this type like GooCubelets at 1 euro. So, if you like puzzle games I only recomend this game, at least, with 50% off (2 euros)\n\n\n[u] Note: Will\tupdate if it receives some updates/bug fixes [/u]\nAlthough it's a indie game made only by 1 person I don't recommend it due to the large list of Cons\n\n\n[h1] Pros:\t[/h1]\n+ You can enable/disable dynamic shadows, dynamic lights and dephts of field\n\n[h1] Cons:[/h1]\n- Sloppy controls\n- Hit detection. Sometimes you aren't visibly touching one of the red bullets, but you die\n- The music gets repetitive really fast (even more that in Orborun)\n- Unispired level designs\n- It's really fast to complete. I didn't finish the game, but I reached level 14 of 30 levels in about 40 min\n- Really buggy, sometimes if you fall to a platform the hit detection disapears and you glitch through it, resulting in a restart of the level\n\n[b] It's worth the full price?\t[/b]\n[b] No.[/b]",
